pretation, using the average as the reference point. This gives a precise calculation that represents the relative difference between the two years' expenditures.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_90aed7e902e1ca9f","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"shell","arguments":{"command":"python3 << 'EOF'\n# The question asks for \"absolute percent difference\"\n# In standard statistical terms, this is: |A - B| / ((A + B) / 2) * 100\n# where A and B are the two values being compared\n\n# Let's verify with the question's exact wording:\n# \"what was the absolute percent difference of these corresponding years' \n#  total sum values\"\n\n# Values:\nsum_1940 = 2602  # million dollars\nsum_1953 = 44463  # million dollars\n\n# Using the standard percent difference formula (using average as denominator):\nabs_pct_diff = abs(sum_1953 - sum_1940) / ((sum_1953 + sum_1940) / 2) * 100\n\nprint(f\"Sum for 1940 (all calendar months): {sum_1940} million\")\nprint(f\"Sum for 1953 (all calendar months): {sum_1953} million\")\nprint(f\"\\nAbsolute Percent Difference: {abs_pct_diff:.2f}%\")\nEOF"}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"developer"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
